d store directory is named in the refusal; init over an existing ignored .claims/ refuses) because they were the findings of the previous gaze on this PR (head ceed4ca), whose result was not recorded on notes. Also confirm the earlier exit-criteria verdict still holds at the new head.\nreview plan: panel; fixtests (script, none), correctness (sonnet, anthropic), redteam (gpt-6.1-sol, openai), exitcriteria (self, anthropic); 12m. A script check settles the five behaviours, with a red control on ceed4ca; two seats from two families read the fix diff ceed4ca..09d6a5a for correctness and bypass; self re-reads the exit criteria at the new head.\nran: fixtests: reported in 11s; correctness: reported in 59s; redteam: reported in 78s; exitcriteria: reported in 90s\nplan check: PASS \u2014 no deviation; the what is settled.\n\nFindings:\n- fixtests (check): all five fixes hold on 09d6a5a and their tests have teeth. The binary was built in /tmp from `git archive`; nothing was built in the review tree. go test ./... ok. Suite results: test_claims.sh 51/51, test_install.sh 45/45, test_hook.sh 8/8, test_init.sh 61/61, test_selfcoherence.sh 15/15, test_integration.sh 25/25. Red control: the head's test_claims.sh run with the ceed4ca binary fails exactly the four new cases (incoming tickets/erg ran, init accepted an ignored existing .claims/, ignored store directory not named, FILE in closed/ warned about closed/). TestMigrateBlocksNumberedDirectory fails on the ceed4ca source (written=1, no blocker). A probe confirms check exits 1 and names the `.claims/9999` directory.\n- exitcriteria (self): every exit criterion of ticket 0307 still holds at 09d6a5a. The fix commit only adds refusals, a hook branch and tests. CI \"test\" succeeded on 09d6a5a. Both erg check tickets/ (head build) and the vendored tickets/erg check tickets/ exit 0. The grep for opt-in or switching-on framing in the docs is empty. Local make check was not run, since it writes build/ in the review tree; the equivalent suites ran on the /tmp build.\n- redteam, consider: src/go/install.go:165. When a merge changes tickets/erg, the hook skips erg check entirely, and the remaining index check only tests that each claim exists. A merge that also updates the binary and brings in a duplicate number (two tickets on one claim) therefore passes the hook. The seat ran the awk program as evidence: duplicate_with_one_claim gives no output. This is a documented trade-off (integration.md says only the index check runs), it does not touch the ticket's exit criterion (an unclaimed ticket is refused), and the next pre-commit and CI still catch it. Cheaper alternative that keeps the full check: run HEAD's committed binary, extracted with `git show HEAD:tickets/erg` into a temp file, rather than skipping.\n- redteam, consider: src/go/install.go:165. If tickets/erg is a tracked symlink to a path the merge changes, the incoming target still runs. Found by inspection, not reproduced. erg vendors a regular file, so no realistic layout produces this.\n- correctness, consider: src/go/claims.go:597. Any directory whose base name is `closed` is taken to be a store's closed/, so a store literally named closed would be warned about its parent. This affects warnings only and no realistic layout produces it. Suggested guard: rewrite only when dir has no .claims/ and its parent does.\n- correctness, consider: src/go/nextid.go:62. maxIDInDir skips directories, so with `.claims/0002/` present, erg new fails with \"could not allocate a unique ID after 20 attempts (concurrent contention)\". Probe: the head and ceed4ca binaries behave the same, so this predates the fix. check names the directory and says to remove it; only new's message misleads.\n- correctness, consider: src/go/claims.go:182. When the ignoring rule is on an ancestor of the store, not the store itself, the message still says \"the store directory itself\". This is wording only.\n\nUnresolved simplify: not planned\n\nduration: 3m05s\ntelemetry: wa